WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:07.118
To multiply decimals, first forget the decimal points and multiply like whole numbers.

00:07.568 --> 00:09.866
Four times three is twelve.

00:10.316 --> 00:16.124
Now count the decimal places in both numbers. Zero point four has one place.

00:16.124 --> 00:20.556
Zero point three has one place. That is two places in all.

00:21.006 --> 00:26.649
Put two decimal places in the answer. Twelve becomes zero point one two.

00:27.099 --> 00:34.180
Check with sense. Zero point four is less than one half, and zero point three is less than one.

00:34.180 --> 00:38.802
So the answer should be small. Zero point one two makes sense.
